  "pivot": "hq",
  "note": "A Bn two up withdrawing by day, normally avoided unless the weather favours it or the roads demand it (OOW3 s8 para 1 p 40; never lightly under En air superiority, p 15). The click is the Bn HQ of the old posn; the aim is the direction of withdrawal, the second click the new main posn (planned), the intermediate posn between as by night (IBB s74 para 4 e p 373). The sequence is the night's reversed: recce parties and non-essential vehicles first; the forward Coys (A, B) move back through the depth Coys (C, D), which cover them, by passage points to fresh posns to their rear, leap-frogging until contact is broken; tanks last except in very close country (MIB s27 para 16 pp 223-224; OOW3 s8 para 2 p 41); no assembly areas: the units move straight back and form columns (p 41). Passage lanes, contact points and a phase line where the responsibility passes (OOW3 s8 para 7 p 43). No rear parties and no programme from last light. Battle Posns are drawn turned to face the En behind the plan.",
